## OWASP Secure Headers Project — example header lines

`src/root.zig`'s tests "external anchor: OWASP Secure Headers Project's own
example lines match our defaults byte-exact" and "external anchor: OWASP's
own Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy example matches our opt-in value
byte-exact" embed verbatim, one-line example header values copied from
`mainsite/01_headers.md` in https://github.com/OWASP/www-project-secure-headers
(fetched 2026-08-01, `master` branch): the `X-Content-Type-Options`,
`Referrer-Policy`, `Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy`, `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy`,
and `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy` "Example" code blocks. That repository is
licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (its `LICENSE.txt`), copyright the
OWASP Foundation.

Purpose: these lines are used purely as a frozen, offline external ANCHOR —
proving this module's own precomputed default/opt-in header VALUES match an
independently-published third-party recommendation byte-for-byte, not merely
this module's own prior test expectations (see the governing-rule discussion
in `SPEC.md`). No OWASP Secure Headers Project source code, tooling, or
design (beyond the cited literal example lines) is used, ported, or
consulted.

Note: the module's `X-Frame-Options: DENY` and HSTS `max-age` anchors are
instead lifted directly from RFC 7034 SS2.2.1 and RFC 6797 SS6.2 — IETF
specifications, which fall under root NOTICE SS0's "clean-room from a public
spec/RFC" carve-out and need no attribution entry.
